WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.940
CHARLES NESSON: Identity.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:13.620
In cyberspace, everyone has an identity.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.640
You have an identity.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:16.570
You make it.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.170
You create it.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:26.860
In an interplay, in an online group of people within a small group

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:36.620
environment, you express your identity by what you say and how you say it.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:42.840
I think of it in the way that I think about poker.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:48.300
Both poker and jury process play around a round table

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.670
with people who are legally equal.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.660
The poker tournament starts with everyone

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:00.970
having the same number of chips, and the actual unfolding

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:09.200
of the game not being so structured, that you

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.100
can tell how it's going to come out.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:18.895
Unless you actually indulge the interplay of the players.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:28.850
Your play will affect my play, as mine will affect yours.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:35.520
And in a discussion, what I assert, what I listen to,

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.470
the strength with which I assert it, the willingness

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.900
with which I take your point.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.590
These are elements of play.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:53.440
Poker breaks down into how frequently you

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.005
play, what games you choose to enter.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:04.530
And once you've chosen to enter, how aggressively you play.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:15.460
One form of poker player is very cautious about entering,

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:24.720
chooses battles very carefully, but when a battle is undertaken,

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.170
it's waged with assertiveness.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:37.180
On the other end of the spectrum, it's possible to be somebody who kind of has

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.730
something to say about everything.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:43.390
Let's see what this hand, produces.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:51.060
But doesn't actually commit very much, and so doesn't risk very much.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:58.920
Well, out of that balance of play, your identity as understood by the others

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:08.160
around the table takes shape, and your force

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.650
is experienced by the others in how you express.

